  "id": "Compound::DB00920 - Gene::5141",
  "verbalization": "Ketotifen is implicated in the regulation of 3',5'-cyclic-amp phosphodiesterase activity through its interaction with Pde7b, Pde4c, and Pde8a, all of which are known to participate in this enzymatic process. The evidence suggests that Ketotifen may modulate the activity of these phosphodiesterases, potentially influencing the degradation of cyclic AMP, a key second messenger in cellular signaling. The shared involvement of Pde4a in this process, as indicated by the participation of Pde4a in the 3',5'-cyclic-amp phosphodiesterase activity, implies a possible functional link between Ketotifen and Pde4a. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanism by which Ketotifen could exert its effects, possibly through the inhibition of multiple phosphodiesterases, thereby affecting downstream signaling pathways. The observed scores support a consistent pattern of interaction, suggesting that Ketotifen may act as a modulator of Pde4a through its binding to related phosphodiesterase subunits.",
